      "problem": "The question's answer is \"That man and his family,\" but the question never says who \"that man\" is. The question only mentions the people who hide their eyes, so a baker could read \"that man\" as one of them instead of the man who gave his child to Molech (Lev 20:4-5).",
      "rule": {
        "link": "prep-walkthrough.md#how-to-word-a-choice-card",
        "text": "Always give context in the question. The story card before it isn't on screen anymore, so the question says who and what. Never \"him,\" \"that\" or \"it\" pointing back to a card the baker can't see."
      },
      "by": "opus",
      "at": {
